.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus","homepage":"https://quarkus.io","size":451357,"stargazers_count":15335,"watchers_count":15335,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":3033,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2724,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","hacktoberfest","java","kubernetes","reactive"],"visibility":"public","forks":3033,"open_issues":2724,"watchers":15335,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls/945","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/945","diff_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/945.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/945.patch","merged_at":"2019-02-21T12:32:41Z"},"body":"Here is an initial stab at creating a test-extension in the core module. There are a couple of things I'm not sure of:\r\n\r\n1. I'm validating the TestBuildTimeConfig and TestRunTimeConfig config roots in the TestTemplate#checkConfig build step. I was expecting that the TestRunTimeConfig fields would not have been set since it uses ConfigPhase.RUN_TIME. Currently that check is commented out since it fails. What am I missing here about how ConfigPhase.RUN_TIME behaves?\r\n\r\n2. During the initialization phase of configuration, all config object fields are initialized to their given default or some type specific default. I have added a mapDefaultValue utility method to allow for the ObjectConfigType to  provide a better choice than an empty string based on the fieldClass. This addresses the problem of #891. I see #877 regarding empty string values passed to the converters. The question I have is why are we trying to initialize non-defaulted fields?\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/945/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/465867518","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/956#issuecomment-465867518","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/956","id":465867518,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTg2NzUxOA==","user":{"login":"starksm64","id":332210,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjIxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64","html_url":"https://github.com/starksm64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-21T05:31:07Z","updated_at":"2019-02-21T05:31:07Z","body":"The current #945 PR has a test that shows this issue:\r\norg.jboss.shamrock.extest.ConfiguredBeanTest#validateRuntimeConfigMap\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/465867518/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"starksm64","id":332210,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjIxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64","html_url":"https://github.com/starksm64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/465900235","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/956#issuecomment-465900235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/956","id":465900235,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTkwMDIzNQ==","user":{"login":"starksm64","id":332210,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjIxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64","html_url":"https://github.com/starksm64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-21T08:02:21Z","updated_at":"2019-02-21T08:02:21Z","body":"The problem is related to this block of code in ConfigurationSetup#generateParserBody:\r\n\r\n```java\r\n            // branches for each next-string\r\n            final Iterable<String> names = keyMap.childNames();\r\n            for (String name : names) {\r\n                if (name.equals(ConfigPatternMap.WILD_CARD)) {\r\n                    // skip <1>\r\n                } else {\r\n                    // TODO: string switch\r\n                    // if (keyIter.nextSegmentEquals(name)) {\r\n```\r\n<1> Map types are hitting this skip statement and not having their children parsing generated.\r\n\r\nFor example, when the map object associated with the ConfiguredBeanTest#validateRuntimeConfigMap hits that skip, this is the parent ConfigPatternMap:\r\n\r\n```\r\nkeyMap = {ConfigPatternMap@2616} \r\n matched = null\r\n children = {TreeMap@2628}  size = 13\r\n  0 = {TreeMap$Entry@2631} \"double-primitive\" -> \r\n  1 = {TreeMap$Entry@2632} \"long-list\" -> \r\n  2 = {TreeMap$Entry@2633} \"long-primitive\" -> \r\n  3 = {TreeMap$Entry@2634} \"long-value\" -> \r\n  4 = {TreeMap$Entry@2635} \"nested-config-map\" -> \r\n   key = \"nested-config-map\"\r\n   value = {ConfigPatternMap@2589} \r\n    matched = null\r\n    children = {TreeMap@2602}  size = 1\r\n     0 = {TreeMap$Entry@2605} \"{*}\" -> \r\n      key = \"{*}\"\r\n      value = {ConfigPatternMap@2606}  // This tree is being skipped\r\n       matched = null\r\n       children = {TreeMap@2607}  size = 2\r\n        0 = {TreeMap$Entry@2610} \"nested-value\" -> \r\n        1 = {TreeMap$Entry@2611} \"oov\" -> \r\n  5 = {TreeMap$Entry@2636} \"oov\" -> \r\n  6 = {TreeMap$Entry@2637} \"oov-with-default\" -> \r\n  7 = {TreeMap$Entry@2638} \"opt-double-value\" -> \r\n  8 = {TreeMap$Entry@2639} \"opt-long-value\" -> \r\n  9 = {TreeMap$Entry@2640} \"optional-long-value\" -> \r\n  10 = {TreeMap$Entry@2641} \"ovo\" -> \r\n  11 = {TreeMap$Entry@2642} \"ovo-with-default\" -> \r\n  12 = {TreeMap$Entry@2643} \"string-list\" -> \r\n```\r\nThe generated ConfigHelper.class ends up with an empty parseKey_rt_all_values_nested_config_map parse method for the map.\r\n\r\nI tried just adding this little hack to see what would happen:\r\n```java\r\n            // branches for each next-string\r\n            final Iterable<String> names = keyMap.childNames();\r\n            for (String name : names) {\r\n                if (name.equals(ConfigPatternMap.WILD_CARD)) {\r\n                    // skip\r\n                    try (BytecodeCreator nameMatched = body.ifNonZero(body.invokeVirtualMethod(NI_NEXT_EQUALS, keyIter, body.load(name))).trueBranch()) {\r\n                        // keyIter.next();\r\n                        nameMatched.invokeVirtualMethod(NI_NEXT, keyIter);\r\n                        // (generated recursive)\r\n                        final int length = methodName.length();\r\n                        methodName.append('_').append(\"wildcard\");\r\n                        nameMatched.invokeStaticMethod(generateParserBody(cc, keyMap.getChild(name), methodName, parseMethodCache), config, keyIter);\r\n                        methodName.setLength(length);\r\n                        // return;\r\n                        nameMatched.returnValue(null);\r\n                    }\r\n                } else {\r\n                    // TODO: string switch\r\n                    // if (keyIter.nextSegmentEquals(name)) {\r\n                    try (BytecodeCreator nameMatched = body.ifNonZero(body.invokeVirtualMethod(NI_NEXT_EQUALS, keyIter, body.load(name))).trueBranch()) {\r\n                        // keyIter.next();\r\n                        nameMatched.invokeVirtualMethod(NI_NEXT, keyIter);\r\n                        // (generated recursive)\r\n                        final int length = methodName.length();\r\n                        methodName.append('_').append(name);\r\n                        nameMatched.invokeStaticMethod(generateParserBody(cc, keyMap.getChild(name), methodName, parseMethodCache), config, keyIter);\r\n                        methodName.setLength(length);\r\n                        // return;\r\n                        nameMatched.returnValue(null);\r\n                    }\r\n                    // }\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n```\r\n\r\nand this does generate parsers for the map children, but the runtime map is still not populated, so something is not matching up in the generated code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/465900235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"starksm64","id":332210,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjIxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64","html_url":"https://github.com/starksm64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starksm64/orgs","repo